# Where the emulator comes from, and exactly which commit of it.
#
# A pinned checkout plus a patch series, rather than a submodule, and rather than a
# vendored copy of a 1 GB tree. The reasons, in order:
#
#   - A pin is readable. `git log` on this file is the honest history of "which PPSSPP
#     are we on", which a submodule's 40-character gitlink is not.
#   - The patch series in `patches/` is then the whole of what this project changes
#     about PPSSPP, in a form a person can read and upstream can be offered.
#   - Nobody cloning this repository to work on the JavaScript pays for a 1 GB fetch.
#
# `make native-checkout` reads this file. Moving to a fork of our own is a one-line
# change of URL here — the patch series does not care which remote it applies to.

